  "domain": "robotics",
  "definition": "Torque is the rotational analogue of force, defined as the cross product of the moment arm and the applied force vector (\u03c4 = r \u00d7 F), measured in newton-metres. In robotics it governs joint actuation, grip force, and dynamic loading across mechanical transmissions, and is the primary physical quantity managed by torque-controlled servos and force-torque sensors during manipulation tasks.",
